好的。Okay (好的). So let’s think about what happens if we try to design a Hash function (散列函数) that is *provably* secure. (让我们来思考一下，如果我们试图设计一个在理论上*可证明*安全的Hash function (散列函数)，会发生什么.) We might try to base it on some hard mathematical problem, like the Discrete Logarithm problem (离散对数问题) or the RSA problem (RSA问题). (我们可能会尝试将其建立在某个困难的数学问题上，例如Discrete Logarithm problem (离散对数问题)或RSA problem (RSA问题).) But here’s the catch: (*但问题在于：*) a Hash function (散列函数) needs to map an input of arbitrary length to a fixed-length output. (一个Hash function (散列函数)需要将任意长度的输入映射到一个固定长度的输出.) And if we try to do something like use a Block cipher (分组密码) in a certain mode, we may get something that looks random... but proving it’s collision-resistant (抗碰撞的) is *very* hard. (而如果我们尝试用某种模式来使用一个Block cipher (分组密码)，我们得到的东西看起来可能是随机的... 但要证明它具备collision-resistant (抗碰撞的)特性则是*非常*困难的.) So in practice, we rely on constructions like the Merkle–Damgård construction (Merkle–Damgård结构) or the Sponge construction (海绵结构). (所以在实践中，我们依赖于像Merkle–Damgård
construction (Merkle–Damgård结构)或Sponge construction (海绵结构)这样的构造.) Yay! (太棒了！) Oops! (哎呀！) I forgot to mention that even these constructions rely on an underlying Compression function (压缩函数) that we *assume* is secure. (我忘了提，即使这些构造也依赖于我们*假定*其安全的底层Compression function (压缩函数).) So the equation for a simple iterative hash becomes: H_i = f(H_{i-1}, M_i) (所以一个简单迭代哈希的公式变为：H_i = f(H_{i-1}, M_i)). Where f is the Compression function (压缩函数), H_0 is the Initialization vector (初始向量), and M_i is the i-th message block. (其中f是Compression function (压缩函数)，H_0是Initialization vector (初始向量)，M_i是第i个消息块.) And the final Hash (哈希) is H_n. (而最终的Hash (哈希)就是H_n.) Does that make sense? (这样清楚吗？) So, to summarize: (所以，总结一下：) a provably secure Hash function (可证明安全的散列函数) from first principles is a deep open problem. (从基本原理出发构造一个可证明安全的Hash function (散列函数)仍是一个深奥的开放问题.) But in practice, we use well-studied constructions and *assume* they work. (但在实践中，我们使用经过充分研究的构造并*假定*它们有效.) And that, my friends, is the reality of cryptography. (而各位朋友，这就是密码学的现实.)

